From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:38:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] DKIM2: an unsigned post leaves with a single m=1 (ruling
 17)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A post with no DKIM2-Signature enters the DKIM2 ecosystem at the list,
whose MTA signs it as i=1.  An ingress m=1 over the author's message put
the author's From at state 1, where a -07 verifier checks it against the
list's i=1 (spec-07 §14.8) and fails.

Ingress now adds nothing to an unsigned post and drops any unsigned
Message-Instance on it; the snapshot records version 0.  Egress always
adds m=1 for such a post, over the message as sent (list From), with a
Recipe back to the post as received, which keeps the author's From
(spec-07 §12.1).  Signed posts are unchanged: ingress keeps the chain and
egress adds m=N+1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
